    "depth": 0,
    "payload": {
      "content": "the least labor capacity at which the marginal return required by discounting and depreciation is attainable - necessary for an interior stationary allocation, though not sufficient. These floors are distinct objects: the average-product peak governs maintenance, the marginal-product peak governs Euler feasibility, and the two peaks occur at different capital-labor ratios. Neither floor determines global selection."
