    "depth": 0,
    "payload": {
      "content": "on a restricted transition class; telescoping then bounds the value of every path in the class. A first-passage splice argument (Theorem 5.2) reduces the unrestricted selection problem to four ingredients: (i) a barrier B M dominating paths that stay forever in the middle region; (ii) an upper-continuation barrier U dominating the unrestricted value after any downward exit; (iii) explicit high-admissible policies whose values exceed both B M and every exit payoff; and (iv) forward-closure bounds ruling out upward escapes. Every path is then either dominated where it stays, or spliced at its first downward exit onto an explicit high policy that does strictly better."
    },
